Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.77,0:00:11.99,QuoteAttribution,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(975,0)\pos(578,248)}T. Hobbes, "Leviathan"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.43,0:00:18.28,Main,FV,0,0,0,,Hey, did you see that stream yesterday?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.28,0:00:19.93,Main,FV,0,0,0,,Yeah, it was so good!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.93,0:00:21.94,Main,FV,0,0,0,,What? A drama? What was it about?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.94,0:00:23.14,Main,FV,0,0,0,,I'm curious now!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.28,0:00:28.25,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,To protect my precious friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.03,0:00:30.47,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,I must protect the class.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.35,0:00:34.01,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,Because if the class is protected,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.74,0:00:36.57,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,my friends will be protected.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.41,0:00:39.22,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.30,0:00:42.49,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,That's not who I really am.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.19,0:00:48.02,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,During that incident in \Nmiddle school, I messed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.14,0:00:53.10,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,That's why I can't afford to make \Nthe same mistake in this class.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.09,0:00:57.95,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,And the answer I arrived at for that...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.95,0:00:58.91,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,was...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.07,0:01:02.48,Flashback,Hirata,0,0,0,,Horikita...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.89,0:01:04.44,Flashback,Hirata,0,0,0,,Shut the hell up, would you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.64,0:01:08.51,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,But in the end...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.97,0:01:13.31,Italics,Hirata,0,0,0,,I made the same mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.91,0:01:15.97,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,We're here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.65,0:01:18.47,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,What did you want to talk about?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.83,0:01:20.15,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Kiyotaka?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.15,0:01:24.94,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,If we're discussing the special exam, \NI thought it would be best to have him along.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.94,0:01:26.67,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,He's the team captain, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.67,0:01:27.84,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.25,0:01:29.36,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,So?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.70,0:01:33.53,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,I thought up a way to get \Ninformation on Class A.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.91,0:01:36.67,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Follow one of them around?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.67,0:01:37.74,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.16,0:01:43.29,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Get Katsuragi-kun from Class A on our side.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.29,0:01:44.64,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.64,0:01:51.42,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,He might hold a grudge against Sakayanagi \Nfor expelling Yahiko, who admired him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.81,0:01:55.80,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Since then, he's been isolated within \Nthe class and lost all standing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.44,0:01:59.61,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,He and Sakayanagi are enemies, it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.09,0:02:05.67,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,But do you think he'd betray his class \Njust to embarrass Sakayanagi-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.18,0:02:09.83,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,He would certainly need \Ncompensation, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.33,0:02:13.69,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Do we have something like that available?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.18,0:02:19.70,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,If we make it to Class A, we'll issue \NKatsuragi the right to transfer to our class.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.09,0:02:22.70,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,We'd need twenty million points for that!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.97,0:02:26.20,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,If the whole class worked \Ntogether, we could save it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.44,0:02:29.85,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I can't imagine most students \Naccepting that bargain.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.17,0:02:32.52,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,We're still only Class C.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.52,0:02:37.64,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And if his betrayal were discovered, \Nhe'd be the next one expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.68,0:02:42.21,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,We'd need to rack up those \Ntwenty million points quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.72,0:02:45.68,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'm not denying that he has \Npotential as an informant.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.03,0:02:48.33,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,But the plan you proposed won't work.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.33,0:02:51.48,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,If we don't do anything, \Nwe won't get any information.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.48,0:02:55.69,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I don't think this plan will \Nget us any information, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.69,0:02:59.11,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,If you get a new idea, \Nlet me know about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.36,0:03:06.04,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Kiyotaka, will you help me?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.04,0:03:09.24,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,I've arranged to meet with Katsuragi soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.35,0:03:15.53,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,And if I did that, \Nwhat would be in it for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.99,0:03:18.07,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,We'd let you join our class.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.51,0:03:22.07,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Once we made it to Class A, we'd save up—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.07,0:03:23.08,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,I'll pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.14,0:03:28.02,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,Your class will never save \Nup twenty million points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.01,0:03:35.42,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,However, it's true that I harbor \Ntremendous anger toward Sakayanagi.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.02,0:03:40.36,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,She hasn't told anyone her \Nfive genuine subjects,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.36,0:03:43.93,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,but if you don't mind best guesses, \NI'll happily give them to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.93,0:03:45.17,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,You mean it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.17,0:03:47.24,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,But what would you want in exchange?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.24,0:03:51.25,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,All I really want is the \Ndefeat of Sakayanagi.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.15,0:03:54.53,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,Chess, English, math.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.53,0:03:56.99,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,These three are unquestionably genuine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.30,0:04:00.13,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,Most likely after that are modern \Nliterature and mental math.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.74,0:04:04.63,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, jump rope and dodgeball, which \Nrequire a large number of participants,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.63,0:04:06.48,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,are most likely fakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.89,0:04:09.49,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Kiyotaka, this could be our ticket!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.49,0:04:13.39,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,No, you won't beat her with \Nthis minor amount of help.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.01,0:04:17.93,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,If I hold back, it might help you \Nfight on even terms, at least.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.66,0:04:21.98,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,The only fields in which I can \Nhelp you are mental math
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.98,0:04:26.18,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,and perhaps jump rope, on the \Noff-chance that it's chosen.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.53,0:04:32.11,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,With Sakayanagi on her guard, do you \Nthink she'll allow you to participate?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.11,0:04:37.78,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,In Class A, the only ones skilled at \Nmental math are me and one other.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.42,0:04:43.42,Main,Katsuragi,0,0,0,,If I'm not chosen, chalk it up to bad \Nluck and be resigned to your fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.84,0:04:46.92,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Let's tell Horikita.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.92,0:04:50.68,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,No. She'll be angry if she \Nlearns we went behind her back.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.31,0:04:53.91,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Let me decide when to tell her.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.13,0:04:56.26,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.57,0:05:05.57,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnGeorgia\c&H717377&\bord0\shad0\fs20\pos(92,31.333)\frx4\fry4\frz351.9}Special Lunch Set                         Cheese Gratin                            Tofu Salad
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.61,0:05:07.61,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.96,0:05:10.29,Italics,Horikita,0,0,0,,Could you come meet with me immediately?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.08,0:05:18.56,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,1961)\an7\fnGeorgia\c&H717377&\bord0\shad0\fs20\pos(92,31.333)\frx4\fry4\frz351.9}Special Lunch Set                         Cheese Gratin                            Tofu Salad
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.90,0:05:15.90,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I have a bad feeling about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.01,0:05:25.58,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Barley miso?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.58,0:05:27.94,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I didn't know you were a good cook.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.94,0:05:30.46,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,It's hardly worth bragging about.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.98,0:05:34.22,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Now, you've eaten, haven't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.89,0:05:38.48,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,May I come to the subject at hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.97,0:05:44.96,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I appreciate the effort, but please \Ndon't use this method again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.96,0:05:48.00,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Very well. I'll think up another way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.00,0:05:50.99,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's not what I meant, actually...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.79,0:05:57.62,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I thought up what I feel to be an ideal \Nplan for Class C going into this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.44,0:06:01.00,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'd like your opinion on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.45,0:06:08.76,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You've really exposed our \Nwhole class with this data.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.76,0:06:13.55,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,This is the answer I came up \Nwith over a week of thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.76,0:06:14.26,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs10\c&H959895&\3c&HFDFFFD&\bord4\shad0}RPS  Best Candidate: Ike Kanji  Chance of Success: 50%\N Piano  Best Candidate: Horikita Suzune  Chance of Success: 60%\N Tennis  Best Candidate: Kushida Kikyo  Chance of Success: 55%\N Ping-Pong  Best Candidate: Sudo Takeshi  Chance of Success: 60%\N\NFinal Special Exam Class A Subjects\N(Chance of success with best candidate) \N\NChess\N Best Candidate: None  Chance of Success: 40%
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.76,0:06:14.26,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs10\c&H959895&\3c&HFDFFFD&\bord4\shad0\pos(330,18)}Modern Lit Test\N 50 minutes\N Rules: Compete over year's worth of subject matter.\N Captain rules: Able to answer one question in test-taker's stead.\N\NSocial Studies Test\N 50 minutes\N Rules: Compete over questions based on a year's worth of geography,\Nhistory, and civics subject matter.\N Captain rules: Able to answer one question in test-taker's stead.\N\N Volleyball\N Time limited 3 sets to 10 points\N Rules: Standard volleyball rules.\N Captain rules: Able to swap out three players at chosen time.\N\N Math Test: 50 minutes\N Rules: Compete over year's worth of subject matter.\N Captain rules: Able to answer one question in test-taker's stead.\N\N English Test: 50 minutes\N Rules: Compete over year's worth of subject matters\N Captain rules: Able to answer one question in test-taker's stead.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.26,0:06:16.25,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I have no objections to the content.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.25,0:06:19.41,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But may I make one request?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.41,0:06:20.61,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.61,0:06:25.03,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'd like you to take on the chess \Ncompetition Class A requested.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.25,0:06:26.33,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.08,0:06:30.92,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,It's true that someone will \Nneed to practice it, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.92,0:06:32.03,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Why me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.73,0:06:36.04,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You seem the most suited for me to teach.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.36,0:06:37.45,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.76,0:06:40.04,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,How will we practice, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.42,0:06:43.54,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I was thinking we'd \Npractice online overnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.54,0:06:46.20,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,That way, no one will see us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.55,0:06:50.71,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,You think we can beat Class A this way?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.46,0:06:54.64,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I don't think they're an unbeatable opponent.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.64,0:06:56.84,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's what this data made me think.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.72,0:07:01.31,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm going to keep leaving things to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.16,0:07:05.29,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,All that's left is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.47,0:07:11.96,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Wait a moment, Hirata-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.08,0:07:14.79,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'd like to confirm one thing with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.05,0:07:19.58,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I don't currently plan to use \Nyou on the day of the test.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.25,0:07:24.65,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,But if we end up with a subject that \Nrequires a large number of people,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.65,0:07:27.00,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,will you at least give \Nthe bare minimum effort?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.16,0:07:30.97,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,You're not going to tell me?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.36,0:07:38.01,Main,Sato,0,0,0,,I guess we don't stand a chance, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.01,0:07:40.11,Main,Sato,0,0,0,,With Hirata-kun acting like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.11,0:07:42.73,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,And with so little time before the test...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.73,0:07:46.69,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Wait, Hirata-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.69,0:07:48.41,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Please, Hirata-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.41,0:07:51.81,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,We really need you for this!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.81,0:07:52.95,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Please...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.35,0:07:56.53,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Could you please leave me alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.88,0:07:58.73,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,I can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.73,0:08:01.41,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Then will you bring Yamauchi-kun back?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.90,0:08:05.50,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Talking with you is a waste of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.50,0:08:06.97,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I can go now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.59,0:08:18.51,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Ow...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.51,0:08:20.86,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,If you won't leave me alone—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.86,0:08:22.52,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Well, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.80,0:08:26.22,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Still skulking around, are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.22,0:08:29.02,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,This is quite an ugly side you're showing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.89,0:08:31.03,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Oh, dear.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.03,0:08:33.03,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Don't mind me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.37,0:08:35.52,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,By all means, continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.89,0:08:39.70,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I suppose you want something from me, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.70,0:08:44.56,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,As I already possess everything I want, \Nthe most I'd ask from you would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.56,0:08:47.79,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,to kindly remain out of my sight.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.14,0:08:49.81,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Just shut up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.81,0:08:51.80,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,You don't know what I'm going through!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.80,0:08:53.34,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,I certainly don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.34,0:08:54.98,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Nor do I want to.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.98,0:08:57.55,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,S-Stop this, Koenji-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.55,0:09:00.26,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Hirata-kun didn't do anything wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.26,0:09:01.99,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Oh, do forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.35,0:09:07.52,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,But you'd be best off forgetting \Nabout your boy Hirata there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.85,0:09:10.02,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,He's broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.28,0:09:16.24,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I've had just about enough \Nout of you, Koenji!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.24,0:09:24.97,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,If you come after me, I won't hold back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.01,0:09:39.19,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,If you don't want her, perhaps I'll take her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.29,0:09:46.02,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Wh-What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.02,0:09:48.12,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,P-Please, let me down!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.12,0:09:49.90,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,I can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.90,0:09:54.08,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,You're heartbroken, and physically harmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.08,0:09:56.58,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,I'd like to mend all that ails you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.58,0:10:00.41,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,E-Er... I... I'm not harmed at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.72,0:10:03.04,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,No need to worry, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.04,0:10:06.17,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Despite appearances, I'm really quite gentle.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.75,0:10:07.96,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Let me go!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.96,0:10:09.21,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Put me down!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.00,0:10:11.67,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,I fear I can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.68,0:10:11.67,Main_Top,Wang,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.67,0:10:15.42,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,I already have you, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.30,0:10:14.20,Main_Top,Wang,0,0,0,,No! Put me down!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.93,0:10:22.48,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,You still have call to quarrel with me, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.44,0:10:26.65,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,You're doing this to hurt me, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.65,0:10:28.31,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.31,0:10:31.31,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,You're the one hurting those around you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.56,0:10:39.57,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,At the very lease, I refuse to let \Nsuch a good-hearted girl go neglected.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.93,0:10:44.02,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Why don't you just disappear?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.05,0:10:54.41,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Hirata-kun...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.18,0:10:58.43,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,You'd be best served by \Nleaving him alone for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.79,0:11:18.72,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Hirata.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.32,0:11:24.11,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Why can't you people just leave me alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.74,0:11:28.12,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Are you going to shove me and run \Naway, like you did with Mii-chan?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.45,0:11:31.53,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I'm too tired.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.53,0:11:33.66,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I don't have the energy to run anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.41,0:11:37.06,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,So, what did you want to talk about?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.55,0:11:39.97,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I want to hear what you have to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.38,0:11:48.03,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You continue to resent the expulsion of \NYamauchi, and refuse to work with the class.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.00,0:11:54.41,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I want to know what happened that \Nformed that worldview of yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.54,0:12:00.28,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,What good would it do for me to tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.28,0:12:01.58,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You'll have told me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.25,0:12:10.33,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,There's a terrifyingly vast \Ndarkness behind your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.34,0:12:16.89,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,It all started when I was in middle school.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.49,0:12:22.65,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,A good friend of mine became \Na target for bullying.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.65,0:12:25.80,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I wanted to save him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.79,0:12:30.76,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,But I was afraid of becoming a target myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.53,0:12:33.26,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,so I just sat back and watched.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.33,0:12:35.69,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Then, one day...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.72,0:12:39.40,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,My friend tried to jump to his death.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.18,0:12:49.19,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,They managed to save his life,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.74,0:12:53.93,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,but he never recovered, \Nand remains in a coma.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.34,0:13:00.03,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I'm the one who drove him to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.87,0:13:03.32,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It wasn't solely your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.93,0:13:07.11,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.61,0:13:11.01,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,But bystanders share the guilt.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.38,0:13:15.75,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I thought my friend's suicide \Nattempt would be the end of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.65,0:13:17.93,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,But it wasn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.36,0:13:22.71,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,After that happened, I saw the \Ngreatest depths of human darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.07,0:13:27.71,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,My classmates found a new \Ntarget for their bullying.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.43,0:13:31.27,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I couldn't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.38,0:13:35.49,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Someone who'd been a bystander until then
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.49,0:13:37.15,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,became their new target.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.71,0:13:44.57,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,And even classmates who only tolerated \Nthe bullying began to join in.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.99,0:13:48.71,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Once the bottom rung of \Nthe hierarchy disappears,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.71,0:13:53.04,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,the student just above \Nthem is now on the bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.47,0:13:55.78,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's a law of nature, in a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.92,0:13:59.63,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I was determined to stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.48,0:14:04.37,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,So I tried to control them through fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.14,0:14:06.41,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You did?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.24,0:14:09.38,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I employed violence.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.81,0:14:13.28,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,No one was willing to hit me back.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.01,0:14:18.85,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I created a hierarchy with me on top, \Nand everyone else at the bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.98,0:14:24.99,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,If any conflict came up, I dished out the \Nsame punishment and pain to both sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.97,0:14:32.09,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I think I destroyed the entire \Nclass year as a result.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.22,0:14:39.73,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,The students stopped smiling and \Nconducted themselves like robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.41,0:14:46.48,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And that's why you didn't like seeing \NYamauchi singled out among our class?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.49,0:14:52.13,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,In the end, I couldn't protect Yamauchi-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.86,0:14:57.25,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I was incapable of bringing \Nour class together.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.83,0:15:01.74,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,To protect one person, I tried \Nto rule through fear once more.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.57,0:15:07.20,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's not Horikita's fault \Nthat Yamauchi was expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.20,0:15:09.65,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It isn't mine, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.65,0:15:11.55,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Do you realize that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.26,0:15:15.01,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Yeah. It was inevitable.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.14,0:15:18.93,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,There was nothing any of us could have done.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.55,0:15:21.09,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That isn't true.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.02,0:15:26.02,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Yamauchi's expulsion, Hirata,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.38,0:15:28.53,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,was your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.03,0:15:33.49,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you really wanted to save him,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.84,0:15:36.84,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,you should have done \Nwhatever it took to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.02,0:15:40.32,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,But I did everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.32,0:15:42.54,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I just couldn't save him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.54,0:15:47.44,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Ichinose of Class B didn't sacrifice anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.03,0:15:49.21,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,But that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.02,0:15:52.55,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Her situation was special.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.09,0:15:56.35,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,She had all those private \Npoints that made it possible!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.81,0:16:01.56,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Then the issue was your inability \Nto spearhead a similar initiative.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.56,0:16:03.81,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,That's unreasonable!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.81,0:16:06.63,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Yes, but that doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.63,0:16:08.99,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's the path that you'd chosen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.38,0:16:15.09,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Your belief that everyone could be saved \Nis a private fantasy of your own making.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.07,0:16:19.42,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But if you want to continue \Nto feel that way,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.42,0:16:22.57,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,then when you fail, \Nyou need to take on all the blame.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.08,0:16:25.18,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's the dedication that \Nthat cause requires.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.58,0:16:26.60,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.60,0:16:28.61,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I was under a mistaken impression.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.34,0:16:35.48,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I thought you were a person of character, \Nwhom our classmates respected.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.48,0:16:37.04,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But that's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.38,0:16:42.85,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,A shallow, helpless student who boasts \Nabout wanting to do the impossible...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.20,0:16:47.75,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's who you are, Hirata Yosuke.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.98,0:16:53.16,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,How long do you expect \Nto remain in your dream?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.42,0:16:57.64,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,This is who you really are, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.58,0:17:01.86,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Those are horrifyingly merciless, cold words.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.30,0:17:05.85,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You're free to want what you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.46,0:17:11.17,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But if you want to save everyone, \Nthe only way is to fight to the end,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.17,0:17:14.19,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,and struggle to the limits \Nof what is available.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.44,0:17:18.09,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If, after all that, someone is still expelled,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.09,0:17:19.96,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,you must resign yourself, accept it,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.96,0:17:22.55,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,and continue to walk forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.00,0:17:26.01,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,It's all too cruel.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.64,0:17:32.15,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Hesitation on your part now will lead to \Nmore and more of your classmates being lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.70,0:17:36.97,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's why you need to keep looking \Nforward and walking to the very end.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.47,0:17:40.68,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you do that, then when it's all over,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.68,0:17:43.91,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,you'll find many students \Nstanding right behind you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.92,0:17:50.80,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Do I really have to bear the \Nentire burden and keep walking?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.67,0:17:55.55,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Then where am I supposed to show weakness?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.93,0:18:00.40,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,When you're struggling, you can ask \Nyour other classmates for help.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.36,0:18:05.05,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You can show weakness to \Nwhoever you choose to rely on.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.81,0:18:09.06,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It doesn't matter if they're \Nahead of or behind you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.43,0:18:12.47,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I... Is someone like me...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.41,0:18:16.17,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,really suited to walk in front of everyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.07,0:18:21.01,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,The person you are now
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.01,0:18:23.18,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,can safely walk in front of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.08,0:18:26.07,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.92,0:18:29.04,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Thank you, Ayanokoji-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.06,0:18:35.96,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That should do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.23,0:18:42.16,Main,MV,0,0,0,,Morning!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.72,0:18:44.65,Main,FV,0,0,0,,Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.65,0:18:45.51,Main,FV,0,0,0,,Morning!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.51,0:18:47.41,Main,FV,0,0,0,,Pretty warm out today, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.57,0:18:54.34,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,G-Good morning, Hirata-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.64,0:18:56.49,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Good morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.74,0:18:59.05,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about yesterday!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.31,0:19:02.78,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I was absolutely horrible to you, Mii-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.49,0:19:06.27,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,You've been trying and trying to talk to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.27,0:19:08.00,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I'm sorry I ignored you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.00,0:19:10.96,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Th-Th-That's okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.96,0:19:13.50,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,I wasn't bothered at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.31,0:19:15.80,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Good morning, everyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.80,0:19:17.93,Main,???,0,0,0,,H-Hirata-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.37,0:19:20.51,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,And... I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.73,0:19:24.51,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I realize it might be too late for apologies,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.29,0:19:29.88,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,but if you're all right with it, \NI'd like to contribute to the class again.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.27,0:19:31.89,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Hirata-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.89,0:19:33.47,Main,Ike?,0,0,0,,What's come over you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.47,0:19:34.60,Main,Matsushita?,0,0,0,,We've been waiting!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.60,0:19:35.52,Main,Sato,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.77,0:19:38.21,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,What happened here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.61,0:19:41.02,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Good morning, Horikita-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.52,0:19:43.78,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Y-Yes... good morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.07,0:19:49.02,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I don't think I was wrong to object \Nto your treatment of the class vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.92,0:19:50.81,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.29,0:19:54.71,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,But what you did wasn't wrong, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.36,0:19:58.05,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Rather... it was one correct option.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.70,0:20:02.22,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,That's a significant change \Nin perspective from yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.22,0:20:06.47,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I'm going to do the best I can to recover \Nthe trust you've all lost in me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.95,0:20:23.49,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Checkmate.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.95,0:20:26.36,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I have a long way to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.36,0:20:31.61,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You've acquired an impressive amount \Nof mastery in quite a short time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.34,0:20:35.93,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I still couldn't win without \Nyou taking it easy on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.25,0:20:40.90,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,No one can beat me when I'm not holding back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.53,0:20:43.76,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,You're awfully confident.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.76,0:20:50.27,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs12\shad0\bord0\frx20\fry\fax.1\c&HE1D8D7&\pos(284.667,112)\frz12.07}Ayanokoji Kiyotaka
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.01,0:20:46.51,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's not confidence. It's experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.06,0:20:50.27,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,We'll call it off here in \Npreparation for tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.27,0:20:51.37,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.90,0:20:53.18,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'll see you tomorrow, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.65,0:20:54.42,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.03,0:21:07.05,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,2050)\pos(320,268)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fscy150\fsp2\c&H171816&\bord0\shad0}Final Special Exam
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.14,0:22:40.00,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(850,0)\fnGeorgia\fs24\shad0\3c&H34332E&\bord1.5\pos(188,20)\an7}Final Special Exam\N Team Captain Meeting Spot
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.00,0:22:42.46,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Kaneda-kun's not here yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.82,0:22:53.27,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Ryuen-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.63,0:22:55.18,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.61,0:22:58.68,Main,Ryuen,0,0,0,,What's got you so upset?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.68,0:23:00.22,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.77,0:23:04.78,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,It seems we made an assumption \Nthat whoever had protection points
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.78,0:23:06.93,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,would serve as team captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.57,0:23:09.85,Main,Ryuen,0,0,0,,If the team captain is absent,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.85,0:23:13.80,Main,Ryuen,0,0,0,,it's only natural that someone \Nelse should fill in for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.80,0:23:14.91,Main,Ryuen,0,0,0,,Isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.27,0:23:17.06,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Well, gosh.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.06,0:23:21.00,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Watching Ryuen-kun, back to the wall, \Nwithout a protection point...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.78,0:23:25.37,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,It appears their competition \Nwill be quite amusing, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.00,0:23:31.40,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Now that we're all here, shall we proceed?
